<body><div class="bar"><span>Revert Creations · Shopify Storefront Audit</span><span>Public pages only · async · no credentials</span></div><header><a class="brand" href="{{ route('home') }}">REVERT CREATIONS</a><a href="#scope">Read the exact scope →</a></header><main>
<section class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">For live Shopify stores with a problem they cannot place</div><h1>Find what shoppers are running into.</h1><p class="lead">We inspect your public store for broken behavior, mobile friction, confusing purchase paths, and visual problems—then give you an ordered repair plan with screenshots and exact URLs. No analytics access, generic score dump, or implementation upsell.</p></div><aside class="price"><strong>$250</strong><p>One-time · delivered within three business days after usable intake · no meeting required</p></aside></section>
<section class="section" id="scope"><div><div class="eyebrow">The inspected surface</div><h2>Five public paths. Three viewport widths.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>The audit covers the homepage, one collection, one product, cart behavior without purchase, and one additional public URL you identify. Each is inspected in current desktop Chrome at 390px, 768px, and 1440px widths.</p><div class="findings"><article class="card"><h3>Functional evidence</h3><p>Broken controls, console errors, failed public requests, navigation dead ends, and cart friction reproducible without a customer account.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Responsive evidence</h3><p>Clipping, overflow, collision, unreadable type, unstable layout, and controls that fail at the inspected widths.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Experience evidence</h3><p>Hierarchy, CTA clarity, product comprehension, trust gaps, and avoidable friction—described as observations, not invented conversion claims.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Performance signals</h3><p>Public Lighthouse and browser evidence used diagnostically. Scores vary; no score or revenue improvement is guaranteed.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div><div class="eyebrow">See the deliverable</div><h2>Specific enough to act on.</h2></div><div class="copy"><div class="artifact"><strong>HIGH · PRODUCT PAGE · 390PX</strong>Variant selection expands beneath the sticky purchase control, covering its error message. Reproduced in current desktop Chrome at a 390px viewport. Evidence: annotated capture 04 and console record. Recommendation: reserve validation space inside the buy-box flow before changing visual styling. Confidence: high.</div><p>Every reported issue includes its observed location, viewport, evidence reference, severity, recommendation, and confidence. The final report contains no fabricated analytics, customers, benchmarks, or conversion gains.</p><p><a href="{{ route('storefront-audit.sample') }}"><strong>Open the complete demonstration report →</strong></a></p></div></section>
<section class="boundary"><div><div class="eyebrow">Firm boundary</div><h2>An audit—not access to your business.</h2></div><div><ul><li>No Shopify admin, collaborator account, password, theme archive, analytics, customer data, or checkout purchase.</li><li>No code changes, app installation, implementation, redesign, ongoing retainer, call, or meeting.</li><li>Up to 12 prioritized findings in a self-contained HTML report with annotated captures.</li><li>Automated tools may collect evidence, but each delivered finding must be reproducible and tied to the inspected page.</li><li>Accessibility observations are not a legal compliance certification.</li></ul></div></section>
<section class="section"><div><div class="eyebrow">Delivery</div><h2>One artifact. One repair order.</h2></div><div class="copy"><ol><li>At checkout, provide the public Shopify store URL and the concern you most want investigated.</li><li>The storefront is inspected without signing in or purchasing.</li><li>The evidence report arrives at the checkout email within three business days after usable intake.</li><li>You decide what to repair, who implements it, and whether the evidence justifies deeper work.</li></ol><p>Do not submit credentials, customer details, analytics exports, unpublished theme code, or private preview links.</p></div></section>
